* Orvel MVP / Core Cleanup Plan

  Product focus: Orvel is a turnos-first SaaS for beauty businesses.
  Target: MVP before/around 2026-06-25.

** Billing rule

   - No checkout as source of truth.
   - Billing source of truth is MercadoPago subscriptions/preapproval only.
   - Official docs: https://www.mercadopago.com.ar/developers/es/docs/subscriptions/overview

** MVP milestones

   - (-) M1 unified availability :: in_progress via core slices; admin availability backend + admin UX/runtime async behavior GREEN; public end-to-end booking UX pending.
   - (x) M2 real admin new turno :: done/GREEN.
   - (x) M3 blocked time form :: done/GREEN.
   - (x) M4 admin reschedule picker UX :: done/GREEN.
   - (x) M5 public cancel by private link/token :: done/GREEN.
   - (x) M6 public reschedule by private link/token :: done/GREEN.
   - (x) M7 minimal admin auth :: done/GREEN.
   - (-) M8 remove hardcoded/test hooks :: current/next; hardcoded/test hooks/fake history cleanup.

** Core cleanup slices

   - (x) Slice 1 catalog/entitlements backend contract and gateway :: done.
   - (x) Slice 2 runtime catalog/entitlements wiring :: done.
   - (x) Slice 3 canonical booking backend + core gateway fail-closed/RPC-only :: done.
   - (x) Slice 4 PublicBookingService gateway-only + TurnoService admin lifecycle RPC-only :: done.
   - (x) Slice 5 admin availability backend-first :: done/GREEN.
   - (x) Slice 6 admin availability UX/runtime async behavior :: done/GREEN.

*** Current working item

    Current/next: M8 hardcoded/test hooks/fake history cleanup, unless Santi decides otherwise.

    M2 delivered `/dashboard/turnos/new` route, visible primary create action from `/dashboard/turnos`, and form create with branch/service/client or walkIn/date/time/duration/notes using backend availability; success invalidates availability and navigates back.

    M3 delivered visible admin blocked-time CTA/form in the turnos list with date, start time, end time, and reason fields. Real submit uses `TurnoService.createBlockedTime`, resolves `businessId` from validated branch/session metadata, requires branch, passes `branch_id` to the RPC, fails closed without branch, and on success invalidates admin availability then refreshes timeline/list. Removed the previous hardcoded current-time/+1h/Lunch break submit behavior.

    M4 delivered visible per-row admin reschedule action `turnos-admin-reschedule-action` that opens the real picker/form. Runtime quick-shift +60min and hardcoded reason behavior were removed. The picker loads backend-first availability through `TurnoService` with context `admin-reschedule`, booking/service/branch/duration metadata, then submits the selected date/slot through the lifecycle RPC path `reschedule_admin_booking`; success invalidates availability and refreshes the list/timeline.

    M5 delivered public manage-page cancel by private link/token. The page reads the token from the URL, loads through `PublicBookingService.manageBookingByToken`, renders a safe summary, shows cancel only when the backend allows it, calls `PublicBookingService.cancelBookingByToken`, shows terminal cancelled state, and maps fail-closed errors including `TOKEN_REVOKED` and `BOOKING_ALREADY_CANCELLED`. Mapper/gateway behavior preserves those error codes deterministically after the blocker fix.

    M6 delivered public manage-page reschedule by private link/token. The reschedule action is gated by backend `actions.canReschedule` with fail-closed fallback, uses the real `manage-reschedule-picker`, queries backend slots through `PublicBookingService.queryPublicSlotAvailability` with `businessSlug`, `serviceId`, and `dateIso`, validates required/stale/unavailable slot cases, submits through `PublicBookingService.rescheduleBookingByToken(token, nowIso, selected slot)`, and terminal `rescheduled` state hides unsafe actions.

    M7 delivered minimal admin auth hardening. Admin mutations require a Supabase session and fail closed; provider Supabase no longer has a local success fallback; productive admin mutations no longer hardcode `performedBy` as `admin`/`admin-ui` and use `session.user.id`; mock session creation is gated to localhost/127.0.0.1/empty host while production redirects to auth; login/admin errors are sanitized enough for M7. Backend migration `20260609120000_m7_admin_rpc_branch_ownership.sql` validates `branch_id` exists and belongs to `business_id` in `create_admin_manual_booking` and `create_admin_blocked_time`.

    Last validation: M7 GREEN by D-O, from `apps/dashboard`: `npm run test -- src/app/tests/unit/m7-admin-auth-hardening.red.contract.spec.ts src/app/tests/unit/m7-supabase-admin-rpc-branch-ownership.contract.spec.ts src/app/tests/unit/turno.service.spec.ts src/app/features/booking/data-access/turno-core-slice4-admin-lifecycle.red.contract.spec.ts src/app/features/booking/pages/turno-m3-blocked-time-ux.red.contract.spec.ts src/app/features/booking/pages/turno-m4-admin-reschedule-picker-ux.red.contract.spec.ts src/app/features/booking/pages/public/manage-booking-m5-public-cancel.red.contract.spec.ts src/app/features/booking/pages/public/manage-booking-m6-public-reschedule.red.contract.spec.ts`; 8 files passed, 84 tests passed.

    Residual risk: validation recorded here is the focused contract suite only; no full dashboard build, Supabase remote validation, Vercel deployment, or browser E2E was run. M8/final risks remain: `branch_id` is still nullable in DB RPCs; mock `setProvider` escape hatch remains; `TurnoService.delete(id)` has a local-only UX risk; frontend still depends on metadata `businessId` until backend tenant resolution; Supabase CLI was unavailable, so the migration was not pushed to remote DB. Email outbox still has an old route/raw token exposure risk and remains a follow-up.

    Follow-up: `mini-cal-admin-turnos-ui.contract.spec.ts` is stale/legacy because it expects direct create from list; new admin create flow is route-based.

** Launch gates / checkpoints

   - ( ) Business can configure basic services.
   - ( ) Business can configure working hours and booking rules.
   - ( ) Business can share a public booking URL.
   - ( ) Public users can create bookings without overlaps or double-bookings.
   - ( ) Admin can see turnos dashboard.
   - (x) Admin can create manual turnos.
   - ( ) Admin can cancel and reschedule turnos.
   - (x) Admin can block unavailable times.
   - (x) Private token/link cancel and reschedule flows are wired in UI and validated by focused contracts.
   - (x) Minimal admin auth protects admin flows.
   - ( ) Checkout remnants/hardcoded test hooks removed or migrated to subscription/preapproval semantics.
